---
source: crates/cupel-cli/src/render/text/description.rs
expression: "plain(&Description::Cli(cli()))"
---
cupel [version] · Cupel grades what a coding agent produced. · experimental

verbs
  init      Detect project roots, languages, and test, coverage, and bench commands; write cupel.toml.
  doctor    Verify the binary's version, the configuration, .cupel/ write access, and needed tools.
  describe  Describe the CLI, a verb, a check, a finding kind, a language, a fact, the support matrix, or a schema.
  check     Run checks over a scope at a depth and evaluate the gate. · pending P2.1
  survey    Rank a whole tree without a baseline: hot spots, weak tests, clones. · pending P2.9
  explain   Give full context and remediation for one finding or check result.
  baseline  Set, show, diff, export, or import the baseline runs are compared with.
  oracle    Add, list, remove, or verify the oracles differential checks compare with. · pending P5.2
  tests     List the tests that cover a scope, with a command to run them. · pending P3.3
  suppress  Suppress a finding, with a reason and an optional expiry.
  serve     Run the daemon and MCP server with warm caches and event streaming. · pending P4.2

global flags
  --format FORMAT       Output format; json when stdout is not a terminal, text when it is.
                        one of json, jsonl, text, sarif · env CUPEL_FORMAT
  --dry-run             Preview what would run or be written; change nothing.
  --describe            Describe this verb instead of running it, and exit 0.
  --config PATH         The cupel.toml to use instead of the nearest one.
                        path
  --profile NAME        Apply [profile.NAME] from cupel.toml.
                        env CUPEL_PROFILE
  --cwd PATH            The repository root; defaults to the current directory.
                        path
  --quiet               Write no diagnostics to stderr.
                        conflicts with --verbose
  --verbose             Write extra diagnostics to stderr.
                        conflicts with --quiet
  --events PATH|stderr  Stream progress events as JSON lines to stderr or a file under .cupel/.
  --timeout DURATION    Stop after this long, keeping partial results.
                        duration
  --seed N              Seed for generative checks; recorded in the envelope.
                        integer · default random
  --limit N             Return at most N findings.
                        integer
  --offset N            Skip the first N findings.
                        integer
  --no-color            Render text without color.
                        env NO_COLOR
  --no-install          Never install tools; the default unless stdout is a terminal.
                        conflicts with --install · pending P3.1
  --install             Install missing tools that producers need.
                        conflicts with --no-install · pending P3.1
  --write               Permit writes outside .cupel/.
  --help                Print help and exit.

flags without a verb
  --version  Print the version and exit.

exit codes
  0  pass         Ran fully; gate passed or no gate. · stable
  1  fail         Ran fully; gate failed. · stable
  2  usage        Bad flags or config; the envelope names the fix. · stable
  3  environment  Missing tool, oracle, or toolchain; doctor findings attached. · stable
  4  unevaluable  Baseline test suite fails or build broken; scoring refused. · stable
  5  partial      Timeout or budget hit; the envelope has valid partial results. · stable
  6  internal     Cupel bug; the envelope includes a bug-report payload. · stable

schemas
  run      https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/run.json
  finding  https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/finding.json
  events   https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/events.json
  config   https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/config.json
  plugin   https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/plugin.json

configuration precedence
  flags > env > profile > cupel.toml > defaults
